# Deferred v2: item weather + weight attributes

**Status:** Gated off in v1. Revisit in **v2**. Do **not** expose in UI until product turns the capability on.

## Gate (use this)

`AppCapabilities` in `AppEnvironment.swift`:

- `showsWeatherAttribute` — `false` in both TestFlight and Production (v1)
- `showsWeightAttribute` — `false` in both TestFlight and Production (v1)

Views/services already branch on `@Environment(\.appCapabilities)` / `AppEnvironment.capabilities`. **Do not** add one-off Item Detail checks — use these flags.

## What is hidden in v1

- Item Detail / Item Add attribute rows + sheets (`SetWeatherView`, `SetWeightView`)
- Item Detail share attribute picker + share text for weather/weight
- Item filter “Weight” toggle
- Settings user weight row

## Still in codebase / sync

- Core Data fields + Supabase sync for item weather/weight remain. Data may exist on items; UI just does not surface it in v1.

## v2 enable

Set `showsWeatherAttribute: true` and `showsWeightAttribute: true` on the Production preset (and TestFlight if desired). Smoke-test Item Detail, Item Add, Filter, Settings, share export.

## When done

Remove this rule.
